                "content": "Let $a$ and $b$ be any two positive integers. Then, there exist unique integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a = bq + r$, $0 \\leq r &lt; b$.\n\nNote\n\nThe remainder is always less than the divisor.\nIf $r = 0$ then $a = bq$ so $b$ divides $a$.\nConversely, if $b$ divides $a$ then $a = bq$",
