                "title": "Theorem 2",
                "content": "If $a$ and $b$ are positive integers such that $a = bq + r$, then every common divisor of $a$ and $b$ is a common divisor of $b$ and $r$ and vice-versa.",
                "content_context": "If $a$ and $b$ are positive integers such that $a = bq + r$, then every common divisor of $a$ and $b$ is a common divisor of $b$ and $r$ and vice-versa.",
                "enrichment": {
