                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_001",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "Hey there! Today, we're going to learn about a cool math idea called Theorem 2. It's about how numbers can divide each other nicely. So, imagine you have two numbers, 'a' and 'b'. A number can be put together by multiplying 'b' by some amount and then adding a smaller number we call 'r'. The neat thing here is that if a number can divide both 'a' and 'b' without leaving a remainder, it can also divide 'b' and 'r' without any trouble, and it works the other way around too! Why does this matter? Well, it's a clever way to help us find common divisors, or the numbers that fit perfectly into different numbers. Let's check out a real example, shall we?",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
