                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Working step",
                        "front": "10^2 = 100 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{19}",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "First, we calculate 10 squared, which is 100. Then we find 100 modulo 19. Since 100 divided by 19 gives a remainder of 5, we find 10^2 is congruent to 5 modulo 19.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_002",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "Now, we will use our result from the first step to find 10 to the power of 4 by squaring what we just found.",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_002",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Working step",
                        "front": "10^4 = (10^2)^2 \\equiv 5^2 \\pmod{19}",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "Next, since 10^4 is 10^2 squared, we substitute 10^2 by its equivalent 5 modulo 19. Thus, 10^4 is congruent to 5 squared modulo 19.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_003",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "After performing the squaring, let's simplify the expression.",
