                "type": "example",
                "id": "2.18",
                "title": "Example 2.18",
                "content": "Kala and Vani are friends. Kala says, “Today is my birthday” and she asks Vani, “When will you celebrate your birthday?” Vani replies, “Today is Monday and I celebrated my birthday 75 days ago”. Find the day when Vani celebrated her birthday.\n\nConsider the following pictures.\n\nThere is some pattern or arrangement in these pictures. In the first picture, the first row contains one apple, the second row contains two apples and in the third row there are three apples etc... The number of apples in each of the rows are 1, 2, 3, ...\n\nIn the second picture each step have 0.5 feet height. The total height of the steps from the base are 0.5 feet, 1 feet, 1.5 feet, ... In the third picture one square, 3 squares, 5 squares, ... These numbers belong to category called \"Sequences\".",
                "content_context": "Kala and Vani are friends. Kala says, “Today is my birthday” and she asks Vani, “When will you celebrate your birthday?” Vani replies, “Today is Monday and I celebrated my birthday 75 days ago”. Find the day when Vani celebrated her birthday.\n\nConsider the following pictures.\n\nThere is some pattern or arrangement in these pictures. In the first picture, the first row contains one apple, the second row contains two apples and in the third row there are three apples etc... The number of apples in each of the rows are 1, 2, 3, ...\n\nIn the second picture each step have 0.5 feet height. The total height of the steps from the base are 0.5 feet, 1 feet, 1.5 feet, ... In the third picture one square, 3 squares, 5 squares, ... These numbers belong to category called \"Sequences\".",
                "enrichment": {
                  "avatar_explanation": {
                    "teaching_style": "step_by_step",
                    "total_duration_estimate": "6 minutes",
                    "segments": [
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_001",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "Let's figure out what day Vani celebrated her birthday using her clues. We need to calculate 75 days before Monday.",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_001",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Working step",
                        "front": "Vani says today is Monday.\nNumbers for days of the week: Sunday = 0, Monday = 1,... Saturday = 6.",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "We start by converting the days of the week into numbers. Here, Monday is represented by the number 1.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_002",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "If today is Monday, represented by the number 1, we now need to subtract 75 days to find out the day of the week 75 days ago.",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_002",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Working step",
                        "front": "Calculate: 1 - 75 = -74\nFind -74 mod 7",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "We first subtract 75 from 1 to get -74. Now, we need to convert this back to a weekday using modulo 7.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_003",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "Why do we use modulo 7? Because there are 7 days in a week, so we circulate through the days every 7 days.",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_003",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Working step",
                        "front": "-74 mod 7 = 3\nBecause: -74 ≡ 3 (mod 7)",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "We calculate -74 modulo 7, which results in 3 because when -74 is divided by 7, it leaves 3 as a remainder. The equivalent day of the week number is 3.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_004",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "The remainder 3 corresponds to the third day from Sunday, which is Wednesday.",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_004",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Final Answer",
                        "front": "Therefore, Vani's birthday was on Wednesday.",
                        "front_style": "regular",
                        "avatar_line": "So, after calculating all of this, we find that 75 days ago it was Wednesday. Therefore, Vani celebrated her birthday on a Wednesday!",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                }
