                "content": "If $l^{\\text{th}}$, $m^{\\text{th}}$ and $n^{\\text{th}}$ terms of an A.P. are $x, y, z$ respectively, then show that\n\n(i) $x(m - n) + y(n - l) + z(l - m) = 0$\n\n(ii) $(x - y)n + (y - z)l + (z - x)m = 0$",
                "content_context": "If $l^{\\text{th}}$, $m^{\\text{th}}$ and $n^{\\text{th}}$ terms of an A.P. are $x, y, z$ respectively, then show that\n\n(i) $x(m - n) + y(n - l) + z(l - m) = 0$\n\n(ii) $(x - y)n + (y - z)l + (z - x)m = 0$",
                "enrichment": {
                  "avatar_explanation": {
