                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_002",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Setting up equations",
                        "front": "1. $a + (l - 1)d = x$ \n2. $a + (m - 1)d = y$ \n3. $a + (n - 1)d = z$",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "Using the formula, we express each term in terms of a and d.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_003",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "For part (i), we need to show that x(m - n) + y(n - l) + z(l - m) equals zero. Let's break it down into simpler expressions by substituting from our earlier equations.",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_003",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Expanding the expression",
                        "front": "a[(m-n)+(n-l)+(l-m)] + d[(m-n)(l-1)+(n-l)(m-1)+(l-m)(n-1)]",
