                "content": "The houses of a street are numbered from 1 to 49. Senthil's house is numbered such that the sum of numbers of the houses prior to Senthil's house is equal to the sum of numbers of the houses following Senthil's house. Find Senthil's house number?",
                "content_context": "The houses of a street are numbered from 1 to 49. Senthil's house is numbered such that the sum of numbers of the houses prior to Senthil's house is equal to the sum of numbers of the houses following Senthil's house. Find Senthil's house number?",
                "enrichment": {
                  "avatar_explanation": {
                    "teaching_style": "step_by_step",
                    "total_duration_estimate": "8 minutes",
                    "segments": [
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_001",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "Let's begin by understanding the problem. We need to find Senthil's house number on a street where houses are consecutively numbered from 1 to 49. The sum of the house numbers before Senthil's house is equal to the sum of the house numbers after his house.",
                        "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_002",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "First, we assume Senthil's house number is x. We need to set up an equation based on what the problem says: The sum from 1 to (x-1) is equal to the sum from (x+1) to 49.",
                        "emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_001",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Formulate the equation",
                        "front": "1 + 2 + 3 + ... + (x-1) = (x+1) + ... + 49",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "We express the condition given in the problem in the form of a mathematical equation.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_003",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "Next, we express the sum of numbers using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series. We apply it to both sides of the equation. This will help in simplifying the expressions.",
                        "emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_002",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Arithmetic Sum Formula",
                        "front": "\n\\frac{n}{2} [first\term + last\term]",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "We're using the formula for the sum of first n terms of an arithmetic series: \\frac{n}{2} [first term + last term]",
                        "avatar_emotion": "explaining"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_004",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "For the left-hand side, we calculate the sum using numbers from 1 up to (x-1). For the right-hand side, we find the sum from 1 to 49 and subtract the sum up to x.",
                        "emotion": "encouraging"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "fc_003",
                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Set equal expressions",
                        "front": "\n\\frac{x-1}{2} [1 + (x-1)] = \\frac{49}{2} [1 + 49] - \\frac{x}{2} [1 + x]",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "Here, we equate the expression for both sides to set up the equality.",
                        "avatar_emotion": "explaining"
                      },
                      {
                        "segment_id": "seg_005",
                        "type": "teaching",
                        "text": "Now, we expand each side of the equation using distributive property. This simplifies the arithmetic expression into a manageable algebraic form.",
