                    "segment_id": "seg_003",
                    "type": "teaching",
                    "text": "Imagine the series is never-ending. Like a raindrop spreading through water, where each ripple becomes smaller. If the common ratio $r$ is between $-1$ and $1$, we approach an infinite GP. Here, the sum is simply $\\frac{a}{1 - r}$.",
                    "emotion": "enthusiastic"
                  },
                  {
                    "segment_id": "fc_002",
                    "type": "flashcard",
                    "card_title": "Sum to Infinite Terms of a GP",
                    "front": "For an infinite geometric series with $-1 < r < 1$, the sum is \\(S_{\\infty} = \\frac{a}{1 - r}\\).",
