                        "type": "flashcard",
                        "card_title": "Geometric Progression",
                        "front": "First term, a = 0.6; Common ratio, r = 0.1",
                        "front_style": "math_formula",
                        "avatar_line": "In a G.P., each term is obtained by multiplying the previous term by a constant, called the common ratio (r). Here, 0.06 divided by 0.6 gives us the r, which is 0.1.",
