                "title": "Exercise 2.8",
                "content": "There are some series whose sum can be expressed by explicit formulae. Such series are called special series.\n\nHere we study some common special series like\n\n(i) Sum of first $n$ natural numbers\n(ii) Sum of first $n$ odd natural numbers.\n(iii) Sum of squares of first $n$ natural numbers.\n(iv) Sum of cubes of first $n$ natural numbers.\n\nWe can derive the formula for sum of any powers of first $n$ natural numbers using the expression $(x + 1)^{k + 1} - x^{k + 1}$. That is to find $1^k + 2^k + 3^k + \\ldots + n^k$ we can use the expression $(x + 1)^{k + 1} - x^{k + 1}$.\n\nSum of first $n$ natural numbers\nTo find $1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n$, let us consider the identity $(x + 1)^2 - x^2 = 2x + 1$\n\nWhere $x = 1, 2, 3, \\dots, n - 1, n$\n\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\nx = 1, 2^{2} - 1^{2} = 2(1) + 1 \\\\\nx = 2, 3^{2} - 2^{2} = 2(2) + 1 \\\\\nx = 3, 4^{2} - 3^{2} = 2(3) + 1 \\\\\n\\vdots \\qquad \\vdots \\qquad \\vdots \\\\\nx = n - 1, n^{2} - (n - 1)^{2} = 2(n - 1) + 1 \\\\\nx = n, (n + 1)^{2} - n^{2} = 2(n) + 1 \\\\\n\\end{array}$$\n\nAdding all these equations and cancelling the terms on the Left Hand side, we get,\n\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n(n + 1)^{2} - 1^{2} = 2(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n) + n \\\\\nn^{2} + 2n = 2(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n) + n \\\\\n2(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n) = n^{2} + n = n(n + 1) \\\\\n1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\\\\n\\end{array}$$\n\nSum of first $n$ odd natural numbers\n$1 + 3 + 5 + \\dots + (2n - 1)$\n\nIt is an A.P. with $a = 1$, $d = 2$ and $l = 2n - 1$\n\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\nS_{n} = \\frac{n}{2}[a + l] \\\\\n= \\frac{n}{2}[1 + 2n - 1] \\\\\nS_{n} = \\frac{n}{2} \\times 2n = n^{2} \\\\\n\\end{array}$$\n\nSum of squares of first $n$ natural numbers\nTo find $1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2$, let us consider the identity $(x + 1)^3 - x^3 = 3x^2 + 3x + 1$\n\nWhere $x = 1, 2, 3, \\dots, n - 1, n$\n\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\nx = 1, 2^{3} - 1^{3} = 3(1)^{2} + 3(1) + 1 \\\\\nx = 2, 3^{3} - 2^{3} = 3(2)^{2} + 3(2) + 1 \\\\\nx = 3, 4^{3} - 3^{3} = 3(3)^{2} + 3(3) + 1 \\\\\n\\vdots \\qquad \\vdots \\qquad \\vdots \\\\\nx = n - 1, n^{3} - (n - 1)^{3} = 3(n - 1)^{2} + 3(n - 1) + 1 \\\\\nx = n, (n + 1)^{3} - n^{3} = 3n^{2} + 3n + 1 \\\\\n\\end{array}$$\n\nAdding all these equations and cancelling the terms on the Left Hand side, we get,\n\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n(n + 1)^3 - 1^3 = 3(1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2) + 3(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n) + n \\\\\nn^3 + 3n^2 + 3n = 3(1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2) + \\frac{3n(n + 1)}{2} + n \\\\\n3(1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2) = n^3 + 3n^2 + 2n - \\frac{3n(n + 1)}{2} = \\frac{2n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n - 3n^2 - 3n}{2} \\\\\n3(1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2) = \\frac{2n^3 + 3n^2 + n}{2} = \\frac{n(2n^2 + 3n + 1)}{2} = \\frac{n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{2} \\\\\n1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2 = \\frac{n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{6} \\\\\n\\end{array}$$\n\nSum of cubes of first $n$ natural numbers\nTo find $1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3$, let us consider the identity\n\n$$(x + 1)^4 - x^4 = 4x^3 + 6x^2 + 4x + 1$$\n\nWhere $x = 1, 2, 3, \\dots, n - 1, n$\n\n$$x = 1, \\quad 2^4 - 1^4 = 4(1)^3 + 6(1)^2 + 4(1) + 1$$\n\n$$x = 2, \\quad 3^4 - 2^4 = 4(2)^3 + 6(2)^2 + 4(2) + 1$$\n\n$$x = 3, \\quad 4^4 - 3^4 = 4(3)^3 + 6(3)^2 + 4(3) + 1$$\n\n$$\\vdots \\quad \\vdots \\quad \\vdots$$\n\n$$x = n - 1, \\quad n^4 - (n - 1)^4 = 4(n - 1)^3 + 6(n - 1)^2 + 4(n - 1) + 1$$\n\n$$x = n, \\quad (n + 1)^4 - n^4 = 4n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n + 1$$\n\nAdding all these equations and cancelling the terms on the Left Hand side, we get,\n\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n(n + 1)^{4} - 1^4 = 4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) + 6(1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2) + 4(1 + 2 + 3+ \\dots + n) + n \\\\\nn^4 + 4n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n = 4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) + 6 \\times \\frac{n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{6} + 4 \\times \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} + n \\\\\n4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) = n^4 + 4n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n - 2n^3 - n^2 - 2n^2 - n - 2n^2 - 2n - n \\\\\n4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) = n^4 + 2n^3 + n^2 = n^2(n^2 + 2n + 1) = n^2(n + 1)^2 \\\\\n1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3 = \\left(\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}\\right)^2 \\\\\n\\end{array}$$\n\nSum of cubes of first n natural numbers\nTo find $1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3$, let us consider the identity \n\n$$\n(x + 1)^4 - x^4 = 4x^3 + 6x^2 + 4x + 1\n$$\n\nWhere $x = 1, 2, 3, \\dots, n - 1, n$\n\n$$x = 1, \\quad 2^4 - 1^4 = 4(1)^3 + 6(1)^2 + 4(1) + 1$$\n\n$$x = 2, \\quad 3^4 - 2^4 = 4(2)^3 + 6(2)^2 + 4(2) + 1$$\n\n$$x = 3, \\quad 4^4 - 3^4 = 4(3)^3 + 6(3)^2 + 4(3) + 1$$\n\n$$\\vdots \\quad \\vdots \\quad \\vdots$$\n\n$$x = n - 1, \\quad n^4 - (n - 1)^4 = 4(n - 1)^3 + 6(n - 1)^2 + 4(n - 1) + 1$$\n\n$$x = n, \\quad (n + 1)^4 - n^4 = 4n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n + 1$$\n\nAdding all these equations and cancelling the terms on the Left Hand side, we get,\n\n$$(n + 1)^{4} - 1^4 = 4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) + 6(1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + \\dots + n^2) + 4(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n) + n$$\n\n$$n^4 + 4n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n = 4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) + 6 \\times \\frac{n(n + 1)(2n + 1)}{6} + 4 \\times \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} + n$$\n\n$$4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) = n^4 + 4n^3 + 6n^2 + 4n - 2n^3 - n^2 - 2n^2 - n - 2n^2 - 2n - n$$\n\n$$4(1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3) = n^4 + 2n^3 + n^2 = n^2(n^2 + 2n + 1) = n^2(n + 1)^2$$\n\n$$1^3 + 2^3 + 3^3 + \\dots + n^3 = \\left(\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}\\right)^2$$",
