                "title": "Example 2.4",
                "content": "If the Highest Common Factor of 210 and 55 is expressible in the form $55x - 325$, find $x$.",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "Using Euclid's Division Algorithm, let us find the HCF of given numbers\n$$\n210 = 55 \\times 3 + 45\n$$\n$$\n55 = 45 \\times 1 + 10\n$$\n$$\n45 = 10 \\times 4 + 5\n$$\n$$\n10 = 5 \\times 2 + 0\n$$\n\nThe remainder is zero.\n\nSo, the last divisor 5 is the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of 210 and 55.\n\n$\\because$ HCF is expressible in the form $55x - 325 = 5$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow 55x = 330\n$$\n$$\nx = 6\n$$"
