                "content": "Solve $8x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{11}$",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "Solution $8x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{11}$ can be written as $8x - 1 = 11k$, for some integer $k$.\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{11k + 1}{8}\n$$\n\nWhen we put $k = 5, 13, 21, 29, \\ldots$ then $11k + 1$ is divisible by 8.\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{11 \\times 5 + 1}{8} = 7\n$$\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{11 \\times 13 + 1}{8} = 18\n$$\n\n$\\therefore$ The solutions are 7, 18, 29, 40, ..."
