                "content": "1.  $1,3,5,7,\\ldots$ is a sequence with general term $a_{n} = 2n - 1$. When we put $n = 1,2,3,\\ldots$, we get $a_1 = 1$, $a_2 = 3$, $a_3 = 5$, $a_4 = 7,\\ldots$\n2.  $\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{4}, \\frac{1}{5}, \\ldots$ is a sequence with general term $\\frac{1}{n + 1}$. When we put $n = 1, 2, 3, \\ldots$ we get $a_1 = \\frac{1}{2}, a_2 = \\frac{1}{3}, a_3 = \\frac{1}{4}, a_4 = \\frac{1}{5}, \\ldots$\n\nIf the number of elements in a sequence is finite then it is called a Finite sequence. If the number of elements in a sequence is infinite then it is called an Infinite sequence."
