            "type": "section",
            "id": "2.8",
            "title": "Series",
            "content": "The sum of the terms of a sequence is called series. Let \\(a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots, a_n, \\ldots\\) be the sequence of real numbers. Then the real number \\(a_1 + a_2 + a_3 + \\cdots\\) is defined as the series of real numbers.\n\nIf a series has finite number of terms then it is called a Finite series. If a series has infinite number of terms then it is called an Infinite series. Let us focus our attention only on studying finite series.\n\nSum to \\(n\\) terms of an A.P.\nA series whose terms are in Arithmetic progression is called **Arithmetic series**.\n\nLet \\(a, a + d, a + 2d, a + 3d, \\ldots\\) be the Arithmetic Progression.\n\nThe sum of first \\(n\\) terms of a Arithmetic Progression denoted by \\(S_{n}\\) is given by,\n\n$$\nS_{n} = a + (a + d) + (a + 2d) + \\cdots + (a + (n - 1)d) \\quad \\text{...(1)}\n$$\n\nRewriting the above in reverse order\n\n$$\nS_{n} = (a + (n - 1)d) + (a + (n - 2)d) + \\cdots + (a + d) + a \\quad \\text{...(2)}\n$$\n\nAdding (1) and (2) we get,\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n2S_{n} = [a + a + (n - 1)d] + [a + d + a + (n - 2)d] + \\cdots + [a + (n - 2)d + (a + d)] + [a + (n - 1)d + a] \\\\\n= [2a + (n - 1)d] + [2a + (n - 1)d + \\cdots + [2a + (n - 1)d] \\quad (n \\text{ terms}) \\\\\n\\end{array}\n$$\n\n$$\n2S_{n} = n \\times [2a + (n - 1)d] \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad S_{n} = \\frac{n}{2} [2a + (n - 1)d]\n$$\n\n**Note**\n\nIf the first term \\(a\\), and the last term \\(l\\) (\\(n^{\\text{th}}\\) term) are given then\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{l}\nS_{n} = \\frac{n}{2} [2a + (n - 1)d] = \\frac{n}{2} [a + a + (n - 1)d] \\quad (\\because l = a + (n - 1)d) \\\\\nS_{n} = \\frac{n}{2} [a + l]. \\\\\n\\end{array}\n$$",
            "sub_sections": [
              {
                "type": "example",
                "id": "Example 2.31",
                "title": "Example 2.31",
                "content": "Find the sum of first 15 terms of the A.P. \\(8, 7\\frac{1}{4}, 6\\frac{1}{2}, 5\\frac{3}{4}, \\ldots\\)",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "Here the first term \\(a = 8\\), common difference \\(d = 7\\frac{1}{4} - 8 = -\\frac{3}{4}\\).\nSum of first \\(n\\) terms of an A.P. \\(S_{n} = \\frac{n}{2} [2a + (n - 1)d]\\)\n\\(\n\\begin{array}{l}\nS_{15} = \\frac{15}{2} [2 \\times 8 + (15 - 1)(-\\frac{3}{4})] \\\\\nS_{15} = \\frac{15}{2} [16 - \\frac{21}{2}] = \\frac{165}{4} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\)"
                }
