                "content": "How many terms of the series \\(1 + 5 + 9 + \\ldots\\) must be taken so that their sum is 190?",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "Here we have to find the value of \\(n\\), such that \\(S_n = 190\\).\nFirst term \\(a = 1\\), common difference \\(d = 5 - 1 = 4\\).\nSum of first \\(n\\) terms of an A.P.\n\\(\n\\begin{array}{l}\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2} [2a + (n - 1)d] = 190 \\\\\n\\frac{n}{2} [2 \\times 1 + (n - 1) \\times 4] = 190 \\\\\nn [4n - 2] = 380 \\\\\n2n^2 - n - 190 = 0 \\\\\n(n - 10)(2n + 19) = 0 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\)\nBut, \\(n = 10\\) as \\(n = -\\frac{19}{2}\\) is impossible. Therefore, \\(n = 10\\)."
