                "content": "In a Geometric progression, the  $4^{\\text{th}}$  term is  $\\frac{8}{9}$  and the  $7^{\\text{th}}$  term is  $\\frac{64}{243}$ . Find the Geometric Progression.",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "Solution  $4^{\\text{th}}$  term,  $t_4 = \\frac{8}{9} \\Rightarrow ar^3 = \\frac{8}{9}$  ... (1)\n\n$$\n7 ^ {\\text {t h}} \\text {t e r m}, t _ {7} = \\frac {6 4}{2 4 3} \\Rightarrow a r ^ {8} = \\frac {6 4}{2 4 3} \\tag {2}\n$$\n\nDividing (2) by (1) we get, $\\frac{ar^6}{ar^3} = \\frac{\\frac{64}{243}}{\\frac{8}{9}}$\n\n$$\nr^3 = \\frac{8}{27} \\Rightarrow r = \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the value of $r$ in (1), we get $a \\times \\left[\\frac{2}{3}\\right]^3 = \\frac{8}{9} \\Rightarrow a = 3$\n\nTherefore the Geometric Progression is $a$, $ar$, $ar^2$, ... That is, 3, 2, $\\frac{4}{3}$, ..."
