                "content": "Find the sum of 8 terms of the G.P. $1, -3, 9, -27 \\ldots$",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "Solutions Here, the first term $a = 1$, common ratio $r = \\frac{-3}{1} = -3 < 1$, Here, $n = 8$.\n\nSum to $n$ terms of a G.P. is $S_{n} = \\frac{a(r^{n} - 1)}{r - 1}$ if $r \\neq 1$\n\n$$\n\\text{Hence,} \\quad S_{8} = \\frac{1\\left((-3)^{8} - 1\\right)}{(-3) - 1} = \\frac{6561 - 1}{-4} = -1640\n$$"
