                  "solution": "Solution Let $n$ be the number of terms to be added to get the sum 1365\n\n$$\na = 1, \\quad r = \\frac{4}{1} = 4 > 1\n$$\n\n$$\nS_{n} = 1365 \\Rightarrow \\frac{a(r^{n} - 1)}{r - 1} = 1365\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1(4^{n} - 1)}{4 - 1} = 1365 \\text{ so, } (4^{n} - 1) = 4095\n$$\n\n$$\n4^{n} = 4096 \\text{ then } 4^{n} = 4^{6}\n$$\n\n$$\nn = 6\n$$"
