                "content": "(i) $1 + 2 + 3 + \\ldots + 50$ (ii) $16 + 17 + 18 + \\ldots + 75$",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "(i) $1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 50$ Using, $1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$ $1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 50 = \\frac{50 \\times (50 + 1)}{2} = 1275$ \n(ii) $16 + 17 + 18 + \\dots + 75 = (1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 75) - (1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 15)$ $= \\frac{75(75 + 1)}{2} - \\frac{15(15 + 1)}{2} = 2850 - 120 = 2730$"
