                "content": "(i) $1 + 3 + 5 + \\dots$ to 40 terms\n\n(ii) $2 + 4 + 6 + \\dots + 80$\n\n(iii) $1 + 3 + 5 + \\dots + 55$",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "(i) $1 + 3 + 5 + \\dots + 40$ terms $= 40^2 = 1600$\n(ii) $2 + 4 + 6 + \\dots + 80 = 2(1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + 40) = 2 \\times \\frac{40 \\times (40 + 1)}{2} = 1640$\n(iii) $1 + 3 + 5 + \\dots + 55$ Here the number of terms is not given. Now we have to find the number of terms using the formula, $n = \\frac{(l - a)}{d} + 1 \\Rightarrow n = \\frac{(55 - 1)}{2} + 1 = 28$ Therefore, $1 + 3 + 5 + \\dots + 55 = (28)^2 = 784$"
