                "type": "example",
                "id": "Example 2.58",
                "title": "If",
                "content": "$1 + 2 + 3 + \\dots + n = 666$ then find $n$.",
                "metadata": {
                  "solution": "Since, $1 + 2 + 3 + \\ldots + n = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$, we have $\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} = 666$ $n^2 + n - 1332 = 0 \\Rightarrow (n + 37)(n - 36) = 0$ $So, n = -37 \\text{ or } n = 36$ But $n \\neq -37$ ($\\because n$ is a natural number); Hence $n = 36$."
                }
