            "title": "Example 2.3",
            "content": "Show that the square of an odd integer is of the form 4q + 1, for some integer q.\n\nSolution Let x be any odd integer. Since any odd integer is one more than an even integer, we have x = 2k + 1, for some integer k.\n\nx^{2} = (2k + 1)^{2} = 4k^{2} + 4k + 1 = 4k(k + 1) + 1 = 4q + 1, where q = k(k + 1) is some integer.",
            "metadata": {
              "solution": "Let x = 2k + 1 (odd integer). Then x^2 = (2k + 1)^2 = 4k^2 + 4k + 1 = 4[k(k+1)] + 1. Take q = k(k+1), which is an integer, so x^2 = 4q + 1."
